cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DirrochaCMS in academic work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "DirrochaCMS: a lightweight serverless backend architecture for small research and student applications"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-25"
repository-code: "https://github.com/marco0antonio0/DirrochaCMS"
url: "https://github.com/marco0antonio0/DirrochaCMS"
license: "MIT"
authors:
  - family-names: "Mesquita"
    given-names: "Marco Antonio da Silva"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-9644-4011"
    affiliation: "Computer Science undergraduate student, Universidade da Amazonia (UNAMA), Campus Parque Shopping, Belem, Para, Brazil"
keywords:
  - "serverless"
  - "backend"
  - "content management"
  - "research software"
  - "Next.js"
  - "Firebase"
abstract: >-
  DirrochaCMS is an open-source tool for creating lightweight, configurable
  serverless backends through an administrative interface. It targets small
  research groups, student teams, and applied projects that need to publish
  editable HTTP APIs without maintaining dedicated backend infrastructure.
